    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "ANIMOL"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Ashley Walters’ directorial debut, set in a young offenders institute, is a strikingly shot and sensitively made depiction of survival, surprise connections and redemption."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/congo-boy-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Congo Boy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Set in the Central African Republic, Rafiki Fariala’s melodic autobiographical feature follows a young refugee who, against all odds, chases his musical dreams."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/florid-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "FLORID"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In this striking British feature debut, a young man living in supported accommodation tries to juggle his musical aspirations and mental health issues."
    }
  ]
